Generated operation description:
1. Data Preprocessing Steps:

   a) Extract the flight number from each row, which will help identify the corresponding airline carrier.

   b) Use an API or database to fetch the airline names associated with each flight number. For instance, you can use the OpenFlights API (https://openflights.org/data.html) or any other reliable source for this purpose.

   c) Create a new column "Airline" in the dataset and fill it with the corresponding airline name for each row based on the flight number.

   d) Calculate the difference between the scheduled departure time (act_dep_time) and actual departure time to determine the delay in minutes. If there is no actual departure time, assume a delay of 0 minutes.

   e) Create a new column "Delay" and fill it with the calculated delay for each row.

   f) Filter out rows without an actual departure time (act_dep_time).

   g) Calculate the average delay for each airline by grouping the data based on the "Airline" column.

   h) Identify the airline with the least average delay as the best performing airline for on-time departures.

2. Code Implementation (Python):

```python
import requests
from datetime import datetime, timedelta

# Assuming the data is in a pandas DataFrame called df
df['Airline'] = df['row'].str.extract(r'(\w{3}\d{3})')  # Extract airline code from row
airlines = set(df['Airline'])  # Get unique airlines
api_url = 'https://openflights.org/data.json'  # API URL for fetching airline names
response = requests.get(api_url)
airlines_dict = response.json()['data']  # Fetch airline data from API
airlines_dict = {code: name for code, name in airlines_dict.items()}  # Reverse dictionary for easy lookup
df['Airline'] = df['Airline'].map(lambda x: airlines_dict[x])  # Map airline codes to names

# Filter out rows without actual departure time (act_dep_time)
df = df[df['act_dep_time'].notna()]

# Calculate delay and create new column 'Delay'
df['Delay'] = (df['sched_dep_time'] - df['act_dep_time']).dt.total_seconds() / 60  # Convert to minutes

# Group data by airline and calculate average delay
grouped_data = df.groupby('Airline').mean().sort_values(by='Delay')
best_airline = grouped_data.index[0]  # Get the best performing airline for on-time departures
print("The best performing airline for on-time departures is:", best_airline)
```
